<title>CHINA: Checkon Group sells 13 pct of HB Int'l.</title>
<headline>Checkon Group sells 13 pct of HB Int'l.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>H B International Holdings Ltd said on Wednesday its substantial shareholder Checkon Group Ltd had sold 116 million shares, or 13.05 percent of the company, through stock brokers to market investors.</p>
<p>Checkon holds 69.11 million shares or 7.77 percent of the company's share capital following the disposal, H B said in a statement.</p>
<p>The telephone maker said Checkon sold the shares in view of the funding requirements of its own future corporate needs.</p>
<p>It gave no further details.</p>
<p>H B shares were up HK$0.03 to HK$0.86.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
</text>
